    bottomLine: "The treadmill that suits almost any couple: tall or short, walker or runner, with no subscription. Buy it if the space and budget allow.",
    description: "The 7.4 AT is the machine on this page that asks fewest compromises of either user. Horizon’s Amazon listing gives a 22 by 60-inch running surface with three-zone Variable Response Cushioning, a 350 lb maximum user weight, a 0.5 to 12 mph speed range and 0 to 15% incline, and a RapidSync 3.5 CHP drive it labels as continuous duty, with a 500 lb-thrust incline motor. For a couple, the controls matter as much as the deck: QuickDial speed and incline dials, one-touch speed and incline quick keys and custom interval keys let each user jump to their usual pace without a long run of button presses. Programs include 5K, calorie, distance, fat burn, hill climb, manual and max heart rate, with contact grips. The listing adds Bluetooth app connectivity with no subscription required, Bluetooth speakers, a fan, a device rest, USB charging, an energy saver mode and a FeatherLight hydraulic fold. It does not name user profiles, so each person’s history lives in their own app. Assembled, it measures 76 by 37 by 63 inches. Our full 7.4 AT review covers the warranty terms. Amazon showed it at $1,499.99 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
