    ],
    bottomLine: "The pick for most couples on a budget under $1,000: the long deck and top speed of the 7.4 AT at about half the price, for a heavier user up to about 275 lb.",
    description: "The T202 is Horizon’s step up from its T101, and the listing is clear about what the extra money buys: a longer 60-inch deck, a 12% incline and a 12 mph top speed. The running area is 60 by 20 inches, the weight capacity is 325 lb (147 kg), and the assembled dimensions are 76 by 34 by 57 inches, with a FeatherLight hydraulic fold for storage. EasyDial controls let you roll the right dial for speed and the left for incline, which is quicker than tapping arrows when two people with different paces share the machine. The listing also gives three-zone Variable Response Cushioning, built-in Bluetooth speakers and a tablet holder. Two things are missing from the listing: a motor rating, and any mention of user profiles or memory, so each user will keep their history in an app. With a 50 lb margin, the 325 lb limit suits a heavier user up to about 275 lb, and the 60-inch deck suits a tall partner who runs. Our T202 review covers the warranty and the maker’s other figures. Amazon showed it at $799.99 on 24 November 2026.",
